<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brandenburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brandenburg is a historical region of northeastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>. Its ruler, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margrave-of-brandenburg">Margrave of Brandenburg</a>, was one of the seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> who chose the emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a>, Brandenburg became the core of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-prussia">Brandenburg-Prussia</a>, which took part in the invasions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-deluge">Deluge</a> and later in the partitions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brandenburg.jpg" alt="Brandenburg" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Brandenburg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
